## 3. Target UX Principles for PetsPage.tsx
### 3.1 Neurodivergent‑Friendly UX
The pets page should explicitly support ADHD, dyslexic, and autistic learners by:
- Using **big section labels and icon‑led actions** to reduce cognitive load.[1][2]
- Avoiding time‑limited interactions; XP and mood changes should be visible and predictable rather than rushed.[1]
- Providing **instant feedback** on actions (XP gains, mood changes, accessory equips) with animations and microcopy.
- Keeping the vertical stack of panels shallow (hero pet, evolution, customise, activity), avoiding nested navigation.[1]
### 3.2 Motivation & Reward Loop
The page should embody a clear reward loop:
- Learn or complete quizzes → gain XP (with a consistent 70% pass threshold).[1]
- XP → level/stage changes → mood boosts and new cosmetic slots.[1]
- Evolution path → clear long‑term progression goals.[1]
- Gacha minting → new pets and rarities when thresholds are met.[1]

Visual design (colors, animations, badges) must reinforce this loop without overwhelming the user.
## 4. UI Structure Specification for PetsPage.tsx
### 4.1 High‑Level Layout
The recommended layout for desktop (16:9) is:

- **Header/HUD bar** (top):
  - Left: small course logo + “BROski Pets” title.
  - Center: XP streak indicator and current level summary.
  - Right: BROski$ coin balance and quick link to Shop.[3]

- **Main content grid** (two‑column):
  - Left column (approx. 60% width): hero pet card + evolution path.
  - Right column (approx. 40% width): customise panel + recent activity.

- **Footer/secondary**: optional mint‑another‑pet carousel or call‑to‑action band spanning bottom.
### 4.2 Hero Pet Card
The hero card should contain:
- Pet avatar art (e.g., Luna the Blizzard Lizard) centered and large.[1]
- Pet name (display name) and species name stacked.[1]
- Mood badge with text (Happy / Neutral / Sad) and color.
- Activity status (Idle / Studying / Evolving) in smaller text.
- XP bar with numeric label (e.g., “415 / 500 XP to Learner”).[1]
- Stage chip (Baby, Learner, Builder, Shipper, Hyperfocus God, Legend).[1]
- Quick actions row (e.g., “View Evolution Path”, “Customise Pet”).
### 4.3 Evolution Path Panel
Below or adjacent to the hero pet card, the evolution path panel should show:
- Horizontal or vertical stage timeline from Baby to Legend.[1]
- Icons or simple glyphs per stage (egg, book, shipping crate, etc.).
- Highlighted current stage and a visual indication of the next stage.
- Tooltip or description per stage (e.g., “Learner: unlocks basic cosmetics and gacha access”).
### 4.4 Customise Panel
In the right column, the customise panel should:
- Show accessory slots grouped by type (Aura, Frame, Badge, Background, Head, Body).[3]
- Display owned items with thumbnail previews and an equip button.
- Provide a friendly link to the Shop (“Earn BROski$ to unlock more vibes”) rather than a hard sales push.[3]
- Show current equipped items visually around the pet avatar when possible.
### 4.5 Recent Activity Panel
Also in the right column:
- List recent XP events from the course (quiz passes, coding sessions, streaks).[1]
- Use icon + short sentence formatting (e.g., “Quiz passed at 80% → +30 XP”).
- Group events by day and highlight new ones since last visit.
### 4.6 Mint Another Pet / Collection
At the bottom or in a modal:
- Show existing pets in a horizontally scrollable carousel.
- Provide a mint‑another‑pet button when XP conditions are met.
- Clearly indicate rarity probabilities for gacha mints (Common → Mythic).[1]
## 5. Visual Style & Design Tokens
### 5.1 Color Palette
Based on the reference screenshot and generated mockup, the palette should include:[2]

- Background:
  - Sky blue (`bgSky`) and soft gradient (`bgSkySoft`) with subtle pattern.
- Primary pet & cards:
  - Lilac/pet purple for main cards and hero elements.
  - Light lavender for card backgrounds.
- Progress and success:
  - Slime green for XP fills and success states.
- Rewards:
  - Coin gold and star yellow for level‑up badges, gacha rarity highlights.
- Grounding:
  - Warm brown wood for floor or footer accents.
- Text & outlines:
  - Dark ink color for text and outlines.

These can be implemented as Tailwind theme extensions or design tokens in CSS.
### 5.2 Typography and Iconography
- Typography: playful but readable sans‑serif for body text and headings (e.g., rounded geometric), with thicker weights for headings.
- Iconography: simple line or filled icons with stroke outlines, matching the pet sim vibe.[2]
- Button labels: short verbs (“Mint”, “Equip”, “Boost XP”) to match the course’s friendly tone.[1]
### 5.3 Motion & Feedback
- XP bar animations on gain (smooth fill increase).
- Gentle confetti or sparkles on level‑up.
- Bounce or wiggle animation for the pet avatar when interacted with or when mood changes.[2]
- Respect `prefers‑reduced‑motion` by offering static fallbacks.
## 6. Data & Edge Function Integration
### 6.1 Required Data for PetsPage.tsx
`PetsPage.tsx` will need:

- User’s pet collection from `user_pets` (id, base_pet_key, display_name, stage, xp, level, mood, activity_state, last_interaction_at).
- Accessories catalog from `pet_accessories` (id, accessory_key, label, rarity, slot, description, asset_url, is_default).[3]
- Equipped and owned accessories from `user_pet_accessories` (user_id, user_pet_id, accessory_id, is_owned, is_equipped).
- XP events and streak data from course tables or edge functions.
### 6.2 Edge Functions Involved
PetsPage must call or react to:
- `gain-pet-xp`: adjust XP based on quiz/completion events, respecting 70% pass threshold.
- `update-pet-mood`: update mood based on interaction recency and activity.
- `mint-pet-auth` and `mint-pet-confirm`: handle gacha minting and unlocking new pets.
